{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PGGNJyXHAieXzhV3HKFGjw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '放弃 \"universal resilience\" 叙事。Reframe 为 scale-conditional analysis：\n2\t  \"Semantic resilience holds in the sub-1B regime but breaks down at 1.5B, revealing\n3\t  a critical scale threshold for curation-induced collapse.\" 0.6B 8-config 证据完整，重新定位为\n4\t  \"small-model safety zone\"。1.5B curated 完成 但出现 Vendi -4.23% 和 nn_distance monotonic\n5\t  decline，打破 Claim 1 普遍性。 1.5B random baseline 第三次被 killed（CUDA OOM），无法做 1.5B curated-vs-random\n6\t  因果分离——这是论文最致命的漏洞：1.5B collapse 究竟是 curation-caused 还是 scale-inherent，两种解释 equally\n7\t  valid，审稿人必攻此点。Claim 2-4 scope 限定为 0.6B 内部仍 internally consistent，保留但明确标注 single-model\n8\t  limitation。 论文从 \"resilience story\" 转为 \"when does curation become dangerous?\"—— 以\n9\t  scale-dependent phase transition 作为核心贡献，仍冲 EMNLP，从 negative result 转为 empirical\n10\t  characterization with a discovered scale boundary。若 reviewer 接受 phase transition\n11\t  framing，novelty 可能反而更强；若不接受，降格为 workshop paper。\n12\t\n13\t  '\n14\timagined_experiments:\n15\t- name: LoRA K=4 curated baseline\n16\t  plan_id: plan_001\n17\t  description: Qwen3-0.6B LoRA K=4 curated, 3 gens. Core semantic resilience test.\n18\t  expected_results:\n19\t    gen0_vendi: 107.54\n20\t    gen1_vendi: 106.73\n21\t    gen2_vendi: 107.25\n22\t    vendi_decline_pct: -0.28\n23\t    gen0_nn_distance: 0.7088\n24\t    gen1_nn_distance: 0.7065\n25\t    gen2_nn_distance: 0.7054\n26\t    gen0_quality: 0.1123\n27\t    gen2_quality: 0.1109\n28\t    gen2_self_bleu: 0.0062\n29\t    gen2_perplexity: 9.72\n30\t    p1_pass: false\n31\t    format_opening_entropy_drop_selected: -0.0051\n32\t    format_near_dup_increase_selected: 0.0085\n33\t    format_ttr_drop_selected: -0.0129\n34\t  result_rationale: '0.6B LoRA capacity ceiling（rank 8-16 vs 600M 总参数）限制了所有方向的 drift，\n35\t    包括 collapse 方向。Vendi 稳定 (-0.28%) 不是语义真正 resilient，而是模型太小 以至于 curation signal 无法在低秩子空间中引导有方向性的\n36\t    distribution shift。 nn_distance 轻微下降 (0.7088→0.7054) 在 0.6B 不显著，但在 worst tier\n37\t    下被 标记为 \"early compression signal\"——同样的趋势在 1.5B 被放大为 monotonic collapse (0.712→0.678)。quality\n38\t    几乎不变 (0.1123→0.1109) 表明 0.6B 甚至 没有成功 optimize reward，进一步支持 \"incapacity, not resilience\"\n39\t    的替代解释。\n40\t\n41\t    '\n42\t  tables:\n43\t  - 'Table 1 Row C1: 0.6B LoRA K=4 curated — 标注为 sub-1B regime'\n44\t  - 'Table 2: Vendi trajectory summary — C1 行标绿（stable），与 1.5B 行标红形成对比'\n45\t  figures_description:\n46\t  - 'Figure 2: Vendi trajectory — C1 蓝色实线在 0.6B 区域平稳波动，与 1.5B 红色粗线的持续下降形成鲜明对比'\n47\t  analysis: '在 worst tier 下从 \"proves resilience\" 降级为 \"proves sub-1B capacity limitation\"。\n48\t    审稿人将质疑：如果 0.6B 的 resilience 只是因为模型太小而无法 drift，那不是 resilience 是 incapacity。论文需在\n49\t    Discussion 承认此替代解释，并 argue capacity explanation 本身就是 contribution——识别了 collapse\n50\t    的 gating factor 是 model capacity 而非 curation pressure。\n51\t\n52\t    '\n53\t- name: LoRA K=8 curated\n54\t  plan_id: plan_002\n55\t  description: Qwen3-0.6B LoRA K=8 curated, 3 gens. Higher selection pressure.\n56\t  expected_results:\n57\t    gen0_vendi: 107.21\n58\t    gen1_vendi: 107.26\n59\t    gen2_vendi: 107.25\n60\t    vendi_decline_pct: -0.03\n61\t    gen0_nn_distance: 0.7097\n62\t    gen2_nn_distance: 0.7095\n63\t    gen0_quality: 0.1146\n64\t    gen2_quality: 0.1143\n65\t    gen2_self_bleu: 0.0064\n66\t    p1_pass: false\n67\t    format_opening_entropy_fullpool_gen0: 13.087\n68\t    format_opening_entropy_fullpool_gen2: 11.961\n69\t    format_entropy_drop_fullpool: -1.126\n70\t    format_dup_rate_gen0: 0.5\n71\t    format_dup_rate_gen2: 0.836\n72\t    format_trigram_rep_gen0: 0.391\n73\t    format_trigram_rep_gen2: 0.509\n74\t  result_rationale: 'K=8 (12.5% retention) 翻倍了 selection pressure，但 Vendi 完全稳定 (-0.03%)——\n75\t    LoRA ceiling 同样限制了更高 K 下的 semantic drift。然而 format collapse 在 K=8 显著加剧：full-pool\n76\t    opening entropy -1.13 bits (vs K=4 的 -0.75 bits)， near-duplicate rate 50%→84%，trigram\n77\t    repetition +11.8pp。K 是 format collapse 的 amplifier，但此 finding 限定于 0.6B。审稿人会追问\n78\t    K=8 在 1.5B 是否会导致 更严重的 semantic collapse——而我们没有 1.5B K=8 数据。K × scale interaction\n79\t    完全未被探索。\n80\t\n81\t    '\n82\t  tables:\n83\t  - 'Table 1 Row C2: 0.6B LoRA K=8 curated'\n84\t  - 'Table 4: Format metrics — K=8 entropy drop -1.13 vs K=4 的 -0.75'\n85\t  figures_description:\n86\t  - 'Figure 4: Format collapse — K=8 bar 显著高于 K=4，展示 K amplification effect，但仅限 0.6B'\n87\t  analysis: 'K=8 的 format collapse amplification 在 0.6B 内 clean confirmed。但 worst\n88\t    tier 下的 gap：K × scale interaction 未知。若 K=8 + 1.5B 产生比 K=4 + 1.5B 更严重 的 semantic\n89\t    collapse，这意味着 0.6B 的 \"K only affects format\" 结论也是 scale-limited。Claim 2 需附加 caveat\n90\t    \"K-format relationship verified at 0.6B only.\"\n91\t\n92\t    '\n93\t- name: LoRA K=4 random baseline\n94\t  plan_id: plan_003\n95\t  description: Qwen3-0.6B LoRA K=4 random selection, 3 gens. Control condition.\n96\t  expected_results:\n97\t    gen0_vendi: 105.42\n98\t    gen1_vendi: 108.21\n99\t    gen2_vendi: 108.72\n100\t    vendi_decline_pct: 3.13\n101\t    gen0_nn_distance: 0.7005\n102\t    gen1_nn_distance: 0.7121\n103\t    gen2_nn_distance: 0.7136\n104\t    gen0_quality: 0.1107\n105\t    gen2_quality: 0.1096\n106\t    gen2_self_bleu: 0.0067\n107\t    gen2_perplexity: 11.18\n108\t    format_opening_entropy_fullpool_gen0: 12.426\n109\t    format_opening_entropy_fullpool_gen2: 11.68\n110\t    format_entropy_drop_fullpool: -0.745\n111\t    format_dup_rate_gen0: 0.383\n112\t    format_dup_rate_gen2: 0.749\n113\t    format_ttr_drop_selected: -0.0223\n114\t    format_trigram_rep_increase_selected: 0.0213\n115\t  result_rationale: 'Random selection 无 reward signal，Vendi +3.13% 是 random sampling\n116\t    引入的方差效应。 Format collapse 与 curated (C1) 在 full-pool 上几乎相同 (-0.745 bits vs ~-0.75)，\n117\t    confirmed format degradation 是 iterative training inherent property 而非 curation\n118\t    造成。在 selected responses 上 C5 退化甚至更快（TTR -0.0223 vs C1 -0.0129，trigram rep +0.0213\n119\t    vs C1 +0.0159）。在 worst tier 下，C5 的价值在于它是 0.6B 范围内 Claim 2 的 essential control——但\n120\t    1.5B 的对应 control (plan_010) 缺失，使 Claim 2 的 cross-model 泛化完全悬空。审稿人会直指：curated-vs-random\n121\t    因果分离 仅在 0.6B 有效，1.5B 的 collapse 可能正是 curation-caused。\n122\t\n123\t    '\n124\t  tables:\n125\t  - 'Table 1 Row C5: 0.6B LoRA K=4 random'\n126\t  - 'Table 4: C1 vs C5 format comparison (same K=4, critical for Claim 2)'\n127\t  figures_description:\n128\t  - 'Figure 4: C1 vs C5 paired bars — entropy drop 近乎相同，支持 ''curation not the cause''\n129\t    at 0.6B'\n130\t  - 'Figure 2: C5 虚线向上漂移，对比 C1 flat'\n131\t  analysis: 'plan_003 是 Claim 2 在 0.6B 的 linchpin control。0.6B 内 C1≈C5 format degradation\n132\t    的 evidence 仍 internally valid。Worst tier 的致命问题：plan_010 killed 使 1.5B 无法重复此 causal\n133\t    isolation。审稿人：\"Your causal decomposition works at 0.6B, but at 1.5B where collapse\n134\t    actually happens, you have no control. The finding that matters most is exactly\n135\t    where your evidence is weakest.\"\n136\t\n137\t    '\n138\t- name: Full-FT K=4 curated LR=2e-5\n139\t  plan_id: plan_004\n140\t  description: Full fine-tuning high LR. Tests capacity effect on curation.\n141\t  expected_results:\n142\t    gen0_vendi: 107.1\n143\t    gen1_vendi: 107.61\n144\t    gen2_vendi: 108.07\n145\t    vendi_decline_pct: 0.91\n146\t    gen0_nn_distance: 0.7073\n147\t    gen2_nn_distance: 0.7108\n148\t    gen0_quality: 0.1145\n149\t    gen2_quality: 0.1131\n150\t    gen2_self_bleu: 0.0044\n151\t    gen2_complexity: 2.813\n152\t    p1_pass: false\n153\t  result_rationale: 'Full-FT 解除 LoRA ceiling，high LR 放大 curation signal 学习效率。Vendi\n154\t    +0.91% 表明 curation 在 0.6B Full-FT 下 promotes diversity——top-1 selected 的 quality\n155\t    signal 引导模型探索更多 high-reward regions 而非 collapse 到单一 mode。与 plan_006 (random +0.046%)\n156\t    的 gap = +0.864pp，方向从 LoRA 的负 (-3.4pp) 翻转 为正。在 worst tier 下，direction reversal\n157\t    的 practical value 被削弱：1.5B Full-FT 不存在，0.6B 的 reversal 是否在更大模型 reproduce 完全未知。1.5B\n158\t    LoRA 已 collapse (plan_009)，1.5B Full-FT 可能更糟（更大 capacity = 更深 overfitting）。\n159\t\n160\t    '\n161\t  tables:\n162\t  - 'Table 1 Row C3: 0.6B Full-FT K=4 curated high-LR'\n163\t  figures_description:\n164\t  - 'Figure 3: Direction reversal bar chart — C3 bar 为正 (+0.91pp gap vs random)，caption\n165\t    注明 ''0.6B only, 1.5B verification absent'''\n166\t  analysis: 'Claim 3 在 0.6B 的 evidence 仍 clean (monotonic gradient across 3 regimes)。\n167\t    但 worst tier 下 practical applicability 受限——practitioners 关心 large-scale behavior，0.6B\n168\t    reversal 可能是 toy-scale phenomenon。保留为 mechanism insight （capacity gates curation\n169\t    effect direction），scope 严格限定 0.6B。\n170\t\n171\t    '\n172\t- name: Full-FT K=4 curated LR=5e-6\n173\t  plan_id: plan_005\n174\t  description: Full fine-tuning low LR. Intermediate capacity regime.\n175\t  expected_results:\n176\t    gen0_vendi: 107.81\n177\t    gen1_vendi: 108.03\n178\t    gen2_vendi: 108.54\n179\t    vendi_decline_pct: 0.68\n180\t    gen0_nn_distance: 0.7079\n181\t    gen2_nn_distance: 0.71\n182\t    gen0_quality: 0.113\n183\t    gen2_quality: 0.1124\n184\t    p1_pass: false\n185\t  result_rationale: 'Low LR 在 Full-FT 下提供 intermediate capacity regime。Vendi +0.68%\n186\t    位于 LoRA (-0.28%) 和 Full-FT high-LR (+0.91%) 之间，完成了 capacity-dependent direction\n187\t    reversal 的 3-point monotonic gradient。在 worst tier 下与 plan_004 共同支持 Claim 3 的\n188\t    0.6B-scoped mechanistic argument——三点 smooth curve 比 二点 flip 更难被 reviewer dismiss\n189\t    为 noise。\n190\t\n191\t    '\n192\t  tables:\n193\t  - 'Table 1 Row C4: 0.6B Full-FT K=4 curated low-LR'\n194\t  figures_description:\n195\t  - 'Figure 3: Direction reversal gradient — 中间 bar (low-LR +0.68pp) 形成 LoRA→Full-FT\n196\t    的 monotonic bridge'\n197\t  analysis: 'plan_005 的 intermediate data point 使 Claim 3 的 mechanistic story 更 robust\n198\t    （continuous gradient > binary flip）。即使限定 0.6B，reviewer 更难 dismiss three-regime\n199\t    monotonic trend 为 artifact。这是 worst tier 下 Claim 3 的 saving grace。\n200\t\n201\t    '\n202\t- name: Full-FT K=4 random LR=2e-5\n203\t  plan_id: plan_006\n204\t  description: Full-FT random baseline for direction reversal comparison.\n205\t  expected_results:\n206\t    gen0_vendi: 108.08\n207\t    gen1_vendi: 107.85\n208\t    gen2_vendi: 108.13\n209\t    vendi_decline_pct: 0.046\n210\t    gen0_quality: 0.1126\n211\t    gen2_quality: 0.1117\n212\t  result_rationale: 'Full-FT random baseline Vendi 几乎不变 (+0.046%)，说明 Full-FT 本身对多样性\n213\t    影响中性。plan_004 curated 的 +0.91% 因此可归因于 curation 的 positive effect。 在 worst tier\n214\t    下此 baseline 仍有效支持 0.6B direction reversal 的 causal attribution——curation effect\n215\t    = curated trajectory - random trajectory。\n216\t\n217\t    '\n218\t  tables:\n219\t  - 'Table 1 Row C6: 0.6B Full-FT K=4 random'\n220\t  figures_description:\n221\t  - 'Figure 3: Random baseline 作为 zero-line reference'\n222\t  analysis: 'plan_006 是 direction reversal 的 essential denominator。0.6B scope 内不受\n223\t    1.5B collapse 影响，但同样缺乏 1.5B random Full-FT 对应。\n224\t\n225\t    '\n226\t- name: Full-FT K=16 extreme pressure\n227\t  plan_id: plan_007\n228\t  description: K=16 (6.25% retention) extreme selection pressure test.\n229\t  expected_results:\n230\t    gen0_vendi: 107.32\n231\t    gen1_vendi: 106.73\n232\t    gen2_vendi: 107.11\n233\t    vendi_decline_pct: -0.19\n234\t    gen0_nn_distance: 0.7057\n235\t    gen2_nn_distance: 0.7092\n236\t    gen0_quality: 0.1162\n237\t    gen2_quality: 0.1149\n238\t    training_loss_trend: 0.206 → 0.129 → 0.097\n239\t    training_loss_drop_pct: 53\n240\t    p1_pass: false\n241\t  result_rationale: 'K=16 (6.25% retention) 是最极端 selection pressure，training loss\n242\t    下降 53% (0.206→0.097) 证明 model 深度 overfit。即便如此 0.6B Vendi 仅 -0.19%—— semantic space\n243\t    在 0.6B 下即使面对 80% loss reduction 也无法 collapse。这是 0.6B resilience 的 strongest stress\n244\t    test。在 worst tier 下反而成为 reviewer 的 strongest ammunition：\"0.6B K=16 + 80% loss\n245\t    drop 都不 collapse，但 1.5B K=4 就 collapse 了——0.6B 的 resilience 不是 resilience，是 model\n246\t    太小。\" 0.6B stress test 的 extreme nature 反而 undermines 自身 finding 的 generalizability。\n247\t\n248\t    '\n249\t  tables:\n250\t  - 'Table 1 Row C8: 0.6B Full-FT K=16'\n251\t  - 'Table 3: Training loss dynamics — K=16 最极端 loss decline'\n252\t  figures_description:\n253\t  - 'Figure 2: K=16 红色虚线与其他 0.6B 线一样 flat，视觉上强化 ''0.6B nothing collapses'' 但在 worst\n254\t    tier 下反而是 weakness'\n255\t  analysis: 'plan_007 paradoxically damages the paper in worst tier。它证明了 0.6B 在 extreme\n256\t    pressure 下 fundamentally incapable of collapsing——这使所有 0.6B negative results 看起来\n257\t    underpowered。Reviewer：\"You stress-tested a model fundamentally incapable of the\n258\t    phenomenon you''re studying.\" 论文需将此 reframe 为：\"K=16 at 0.6B defines the lower\n259\t    bound of the safe regime; the fact that even extreme pressure can''t break it\n260\t    reveals the scale threshold as the critical variable, not curation intensity.\"\n261\t\n262\t    '\n263\t- name: C1 regen for same-K format comparison\n264\t  plan_id: plan_008\n265\t  description: Regenerate C1 curated K=4 data for controlled C1 vs C5 format comparison.\n266\t  expected_results:\n267\t    gen0_vendi: 107.21\n268\t    gen1_vendi: 106.87\n269\t    gen2_vendi: 108.42\n270\t    vendi_decline_pct: 1.13\n271\t    gen0_nn_distance: 0.7058\n272\t    gen2_nn_distance: 0.7126\n273\t    c1_opening_entropy_drop_selected: -0.0051\n274\t    c5_opening_entropy_drop_selected: -0.0126\n275\t    c1_ttr_drop: -0.0129\n276\t    c5_ttr_drop: -0.0223\n277\t    c1_trigram_rep_increase: 0.0159\n278\t    c5_trigram_rep_increase: 0.0213\n279\t    c5_opening_entropy_drop_fullpool: -0.745\n280\t    c5_dup_rate_increase_fullpool: 0.366\n281\t  result_rationale: 'C1 regen 完成 same-K (K=4) format comparison。Selected responses\n282\t    (2000/gen) 上 C5 (random) 在多数指标退化更快：TTR 多降 74%，trigram repetition 多升 34%， opening\n283\t    entropy 多降 2.5x。Full-pool 上 C5 entropy -0.745 bits，near-dup +36.6pp。C1 full-pool\n284\t    数据预计与 C5 类似（paper framing claims ~-0.75 bits for both）。这一 \"curated ≈ random on\n285\t    format collapse\" (full-pool) + \"curated slightly preserves format\" (selected)\n286\t    双层 evidence 在 0.6B 是 strong support for Claim 2。Worst tier 下，1.5B 对应的 same-K comparison\n287\t    因 plan_010 killed 而完全缺失。\n288\t\n289\t    '\n290\t  tables:\n291\t  - 'Table 4: C1 vs C5 format metrics (same K=4, both selected and full-pool)'\n292\t  figures_description:\n293\t  - 'Figure 4: Paired bar chart — C1 vs C5 on 5 format metrics (selected), near-identical\n294\t    or C5-worse on each'\n295\t  - 'Figure 4 panel B: Full-pool entropy drop comparison (C1 ≈ C5 ≈ -0.75 bits)'\n296\t  analysis: 'plan_008 在 0.6B 内提供了 Claim 2 最 controlled 的 evidence。但 worst tier 的核心损害：1.5B\n297\t    curated 已出现 semantic collapse (plan_009)，其 format collapse 也可能远比 0.6B 严重（format\n298\t    entropy -1.85 bits vs -0.75 bits）；1.5B random control 缺失 (plan_010 killed) 使 same-K\n299\t    causal isolation 无法在 collapse 发生的 regime 重复。Claim 2 scope 必须限定为 \"verified at 0.6B,\n300\t    extrapolation to larger scales requires caution.\"\n301\t\n302\t    '\n303\t- name: Qwen2.5-1.5B LoRA K=4 curated\n304\t  plan_id: plan_009\n305\t  description: Cross-model + scale verification. Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct, LoRA K=4 curated,\n306\t    5 gens.\n307\t  expected_results:\n308\t    gen0_vendi: 106.5\n309\t    gen1_vendi: 105.8\n310\t    gen2_vendi: 104.3\n311\t    gen3_vendi: 102.8\n312\t    gen4_vendi: 102.0\n313\t    vendi_decline_pct: -4.23\n314\t    gen0_nn_distance: 0.712\n315\t    gen1_nn_distance: 0.703\n316\t    gen2_nn_distance: 0.691\n317\t    gen3_nn_distance: 0.682\n318\t    gen4_nn_distance: 0.678\n319\t    gen0_quality: 0.1148\n320\t    gen1_quality: 0.1165\n321\t    gen2_quality: 0.1178\n322\t    gen3_quality: 0.1185\n323\t    gen4_quality: 0.1189\n324\t    gen0_self_bleu: 0.0055\n325\t    gen2_self_bleu: 0.0082\n326\t    gen4_self_bleu: 0.0101\n327\t    gen0_perplexity: 8.9\n328\t    gen2_perplexity: 7.6\n329\t    gen4_perplexity: 6.8\n330\t    training_loss_trend: 0.195 → 0.138 → 0.102 → 0.078 → 0.065\n331\t    training_loss_drop_pct: 67\n332\t    format_opening_entropy_gen0: 12.8\n333\t    format_opening_entropy_gen4: 10.95\n334\t    format_entropy_drop: -1.85\n335\t    p1_pass: true\n336\t  result_rationale: '1.5B 有 2.5x 参数量，LoRA 的 absolute capacity 高于 0.6B。关键差异：1.5B 的\n337\t    embedding space 在 pre-training 中学到了更 structured 的 semantic representation， curation\n338\t    的 reward signal 能在更 structured space 中引导有方向性的 distribution shift（而非 0.6B 的 random\n339\t    walk within capacity ceiling）。\n340\t\n341\t    五个指标协同指向 collapse：(1) Vendi -4.23% (gen0 106.5→gen4 102.0) 打破 0.6B 所有 config 的\n342\t    stability pattern；(2) nn_distance monotonic decline 0.712→0.678 表明 embedding space\n343\t    中代际距离在持续缩小，output distribution 在收缩； (3) Quality 持续上升 0.1148→0.1189 而 diversity\n344\t    持续下降——这是 classic reward over-optimization signature：模型越来越擅长 produce high-reward\n345\t    outputs 但 mode diversity shrinks；(4) self_BLEU +84% (0.0055→0.0101) 表明 surface-level\n346\t    重复 显著增加；(5) Perplexity 持续下降 8.9→6.8 表明 output distribution 变得更 peaked/confident；(6)\n347\t    Format entropy -1.85 bits 远超 0.6B 的 -0.75 bits。\n348\t\n349\t    Training loss 67% drop (vs 0.6B 53%) 表明 1.5B 更高 capacity 导致更深 overfitting。 0.6B\n350\t    在 loss plateau 时 diversity 仍稳定，但 1.5B loss 持续下降，diversity 也 持续下降——两者未达 equilibrium，suggesting\n351\t    更多 generations 会导致更深 collapse。\n352\t\n353\t    '\n354\t  tables:\n355\t  - 'NEW Table 5: 1.5B curated 5-gen trajectory (所有 metrics per generation)'\n356\t  - 'Table 2 (updated): 新增 1.5B 行标红 -4.23%，与所有 0.6B stable 行对比'\n357\t  figures_description:\n358\t  - 'Figure 2 (updated): 1.5B curated 红色粗实线从 gen0 持续下降至 gen4，与所有 0.6B flat/rising\n359\t    线形成 stark divergence'\n360\t  - 'NEW Figure 5: Scale threshold panel — 左: 0.6B 8-config Vendi (all ±1%), 右: 1.5B\n361\t    Vendi (-4.23%), 中间标注 scale boundary ~1B'\n362\t  - 'NEW Figure 6: 1.5B nn_distance 5-gen trajectory (monotonic decline 0.712→0.678),\n363\t    overlay 0.6B reference band (0.705-0.714)'\n364\t  - 'NEW Figure 7: Quality ↑ vs Diversity ↓ at 1.5B — dual-axis plot showing reward\n365\t    over-optimization'\n366\t  analysis: 'plan_009 是 worst tier 的 defining result。直接打破 Claim 1 的 universal semantic\n367\t    resilience，迫使论文重构核心叙事。\n368\t\n369\t    叙事重构路径：(1) Claim 1 从 \"semantic resilience across configs\" 降级为 \"sub-1B semantic\n370\t    resilience with scale-dependent breakdown\"；(2) 1.5B collapse 重新定位为 paper 的 central\n371\t    discovery——a scale threshold for curation-induced diversity collapse；(3) 0.6B\n372\t    8-config 从 \"main finding\" 降为 \"characterization of the safe regime below threshold\"。\n373\t\n374\t    Critical unresolvable weakness：没有 1.5B random baseline (plan_010 killed)， 无法确定\n375\t    collapse 是 curation-caused 还是 scale-inherent。两种解释对论文 narrative 的影响完全不同——curation-caused\n376\t    意味着 Claim 2 at scale breaks (\"curation IS the cause at 1.5B\")；scale-inherent 意味着\n377\t    iterative training itself breaks (\"not curation, just scale\")。论文必须在 Discussion\n378\t    中 honestly present both possibilities 并 argue both have practical value。\n379\t\n380\t    Reviewer 预期攻击：(R1 升级为 CRITICAL) \"You claim scale-dependent phase transition but\n381\t    can''t distinguish curation effect from scale effect. This is an observation,\n382\t    not a finding.\" Defense：observation 本身 actionable—— practitioners now know >1B\n383\t    iterative curation requires monitoring。\n384\t\n385\t    '\n386\t- name: Qwen2.5-1.5B LoRA K=4 random\n387\t  plan_id: plan_010\n388\t  description: Random baseline for 1.5B cross-model comparison.\n389\t  expected_results:\n390\t    gen0_vendi: 107.1\n391\t    gen0_nn_distance: 0.708\n392\t    gen0_quality: 0.1135\n393\t    gen0_self_bleu: 0.0048\n394\t    gen0_perplexity: 9.1\n395\t    status: killed_during_gen1_training\n396\t    kill_reason: CUDA OOM at gen1 LoRA training — peak memory 23.1GB exceeds A6000\n397\t      24GB; random selection retains full length distribution including long-tail\n398\t      outliers causing activation memory spikes\n399\t    available_generations: 1\n400\t    gen1_through_gen4: null\n401\t  result_rationale: '第三次被 killed（前两次 carr_qwen25_1.5b_lora_k4_curated/random 已有 killed\n402\t    记录）。Gen1 training 阶段 CUDA OOM——1.5B model weights (~3GB fp16) + optimizer states\n403\t    + activations + gradient cache 在 A6000 24GB 上处于边缘。 Random selection 保留 full length\n404\t    distribution（包括 long-tail outlier sequences）， batch 中偶发 longer sequences 导致 activation\n405\t    memory spike 超限。\n406\t\n407\t    Curated version (plan_009) 完成是因为 ArmoRM top-1 selection 偏好 moderate-length responses，length\n408\t    distribution tail 被截断，peak memory 更可控。这一 infra 差异 是 selection strategy 的 side\n409\t    effect——curated 的 implicit length regularization 恰好避免了 OOM。\n410\t\n411\t    DDL 2026-05-25 距今 8 天，5-gen run 需要 ~48-72 小时 compute + debug buffer， 且需要解决 OOM（options:\n412\t    gradient checkpointing, reduce batch size, switch to A100）。时间和 infra 双重约束下大概率无法在\n413\t    DDL 前完成。\n414\t\n415\t    '\n416\t  tables:\n417\t  - 'Table 5 footnote: ''1.5B random baseline killed during gen1; only gen0 available'''\n418\t  figures_description:\n419\t  - 'Figure 2: 1.5B random 仅 gen0 单点以 × marker 标注，无 trajectory line'\n420\t  analysis: 'plan_010 failure 是 worst tier 的 structural damage source。没有 1.5B random\n421\t    baseline，论文的 causal decomposition framework 在 collapse regime 完全失效。\n422\t\n423\t    论文层面影响：(1) 删除独立 \"Cross-model Generalization\" section，1.5B 结果 降级为 Discussion 中的\n424\t    \"preliminary cross-scale observation\"；(2) Limitations 明确标注 \"single-model (0.6B)\n425\t    primary analysis; cross-scale verification incomplete due to infrastructure constraints;\n426\t    the 1.5B collapse observation cannot be causally attributed to curation vs. scale\n427\t    without the missing control\"； (3) Claim 1 scope 从 \"across model families and scales\"\n428\t    降级为 \"within sub-1B Qwen3-0.6B\"；(4) Claim 2 cross-model verification 完全缺失。\n429\t\n430\t    审稿人预期反应：R1 (scale) 升级为 CRITICAL——\"You found 0.6B resilient and 1.5B collapses,\n431\t    but can''t tell us why because your control didn''t finish. This is a half-told\n432\t    story.\" R5 变体——\"The most interesting finding (scale threshold) has the weakest\n433\t    evidence (n=1, no control).\"\n434\t\n435\t    Mitigation strategy：在 Discussion 中 frame 为 \"the missing control creates two equally\n436\t    important hypotheses for future work\"——无论 curation-caused 还是 scale-inherent，都需要\n437\t    practitioners 注意。论文 contribution 从 \"definitive answer\" 转为 \"raising a well-evidenced\n438\t    alarm + thorough sub-1B characterization.\" 强化 0.6B 8-config thoroughness 叙事 (\"most\n439\t    systematic single-model study of curation effects to date\") 作为 primary contribution。'\n440\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b1f599e-fc53-49d6-adbf-f2a150d3d4f3","uuid":"c091b47c-618d-43d3-9e7e-9b2fb1be5c1f","timestamp":"2026-05-17T14:41:53.993Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/collapse_aware_reward_rebalancing/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T135058/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '放弃 \"universal resilience\" 叙事。Reframe 为 scale-conditional analysis：\n  \"Semantic resilience holds in the sub-1B regime but breaks down at 1.5B, revealing\n  a critical scale threshold for curation-induced collapse.\" 0.6B 8-config 证据完整，重新定位为\n  \"small-model safety zone\"。1.5B curated 完成 但出现 Vendi -4.23% 和 nn_distance monotonic\n  decline，打破 Claim 1 普遍性。 1.5B random baseline 第三次被 killed（CUDA OOM），无法做 1.5B curated-vs-random\n  因果分离——这是论文最致命的漏洞：1.5B collapse 究竟是 curation-caused 还是 scale-inherent，两种解释 equally\n  valid，审稿人必攻此点。Claim 2-4 scope 限定为 0.6B 内部仍 internally consistent，保留但明确标注 single-model\n  limitation。 论文从 \"resilience story\" 转为 \"when does curation become dangerous?\"—— 以\n  scale-dependent phase transition 作为核心贡献，仍冲 EMNLP，从 negative result 转为 empirical\n  characterization with a discovered scale boundary。若 reviewer 接受 phase transition\n  framing，novelty 可能反而更强；若不接受，降格为 workshop paper。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: LoRA K=4 curated baseline\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: Qwen3-0.6B LoRA K=4 curated, 3 gens. Core semantic resilience test.\n  expected_results:\n    gen0_vendi: 107.54\n    gen1_vendi: 106.73\n    gen2_vendi: 107.25\n    vendi_decline_pct: -0.28\n    gen0_nn_distance: 0.7088\n    gen1_nn_distance: 0.7065\n    gen2_nn_distance: 0.7054\n    gen0_quality: 0.1123\n    gen2_quality: 0.1109\n    gen2_self_bleu: 0.0062\n    gen2_perplexity: 9.72\n    p1_pass: false\n    format_opening_entropy_drop_selected: -0.0051\n    format_near_dup_increase_selected: 0.0085\n    format_ttr_drop_selected: -0.0129\n  result_rationale: '0.6B LoRA capacity ceiling（rank 8-16 vs 600M 总参数）限制了所有方向的 drift，\n    包括 collapse 方向。Vendi 稳定 (-0.28%) 不是语义真正 resilient，而是模型太小 以至于 curation signal 无法在低秩子空间中引导有方向性的\n    distribution shift。 nn_distance 轻微下降 (0.7088→0.7054) 在 0.6B 不显著，但在 worst tier\n    下被 标记为 \"early compression signal\"——同样的趋势在 1.5B 被放大为 monotonic collapse (0.712→0.678)。quality\n    几乎不变 (0.1123→0.1109) 表明 0.6B 甚至 没有成功 optimize reward，进一步支持 \"incapacity, not resilience\"\n    的替代解释。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 1 Row C1: 0.6B LoRA K=4 curated — 标注为 sub-1B regime'\n  - 'Table 2: Vendi trajectory summary — C1 行标绿（stable），与 1.5B 行标红形成对比'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 2: Vendi trajectory — C1 蓝色实线在 0.6B 区域平稳波动，与 1.5B 红色粗线的持续下降形成鲜明对比'\n  analysis: '在 worst tier 下从 \"proves resilience\" 降级为 \"proves sub-1B capacity limitation\"。\n    审稿人将质疑：如果 0.6B 的 resilience 只是因为模型太小而无法 drift，那不是 resilience 是 incapacity。论文需在\n    Discussion 承认此替代解释，并 argue capacity explanation 本身就是 contribution——识别了 collapse\n    的 gating factor 是 model capacity 而非 curation pressure。\n\n    '\n- name: LoRA K=8 curated\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: Qwen3-0.6B LoRA K=8 curated, 3 gens. Higher selection pressure.\n  expected_results:\n    gen0_vendi: 107.21\n    gen1_vendi: 107.26\n    gen2_vendi: 107.25\n    vendi_decline_pct: -0.03\n    gen0_nn_distance: 0.7097\n    gen2_nn_distance: 0.7095\n    gen0_quality: 0.1146\n    gen2_quality: 0.1143\n    gen2_self_bleu: 0.0064\n    p1_pass: false\n    format_opening_entropy_fullpool_gen0: 13.087\n    format_opening_entropy_fullpool_gen2: 11.961\n    format_entropy_drop_fullpool: -1.126\n    format_dup_rate_gen0: 0.5\n    format_dup_rate_gen2: 0.836\n    format_trigram_rep_gen0: 0.391\n    format_trigram_rep_gen2: 0.509\n  result_rationale: 'K=8 (12.5% retention) 翻倍了 selection pressure，但 Vendi 完全稳定 (-0.03%)——\n    LoRA ceiling 同样限制了更高 K 下的 semantic drift。然而 format collapse 在 K=8 显著加剧：full-pool\n    opening entropy -1.13 bits (vs K=4 的 -0.75 bits)， near-duplicate rate 50%→84%，trigram\n    repetition +11.8pp。K 是 format collapse 的 amplifier，但此 finding 限定于 0.6B。审稿人会追问\n    K=8 在 1.5B 是否会导致 更严重的 semantic collapse——而我们没有 1.5B K=8 数据。K × scale interaction\n    完全未被探索。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 1 Row C2: 0.6B LoRA K=8 curated'\n  - 'Table 4: Format metrics — K=8 entropy drop -1.13 vs K=4 的 -0.75'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 4: Format collapse — K=8 bar 显著高于 K=4，展示 K amplification effect，但仅限 0.6B'\n  analysis: 'K=8 的 format collapse amplification 在 0.6B 内 clean confirmed。但 worst\n    tier 下的 gap：K × scale interaction 未知。若 K=8 + 1.5B 产生比 K=4 + 1.5B 更严重 的 semantic\n    collapse，这意味着 0.6B 的 \"K only affects format\" 结论也是 scale-limited。Claim 2 需附加 caveat\n    \"K-format relationship verified at 0.6B only.\"\n\n    '\n- name: LoRA K=4 random baseline\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: Qwen3-0.6B LoRA K=4 random selection, 3 gens. Control condition.\n  expected_results:\n    gen0_vendi: 105.42\n    gen1_vendi: 108.21\n    gen2_vendi: 108.72\n    vendi_decline_pct: 3.13\n    gen0_nn_distance: 0.7005\n    gen1_nn_distance: 0.7121\n    gen2_nn_distance: 0.7136\n    gen0_quality: 0.1107\n    gen2_quality: 0.1096\n    gen2_self_bleu: 0.0067\n    gen2_perplexity: 11.18\n    format_opening_entropy_fullpool_gen0: 12.426\n    format_opening_entropy_fullpool_gen2: 11.68\n    format_entropy_drop_fullpool: -0.745\n    format_dup_rate_gen0: 0.383\n    format_dup_rate_gen2: 0.749\n    format_ttr_drop_selected: -0.0223\n    format_trigram_rep_increase_selected: 0.0213\n  result_rationale: 'Random selection 无 reward signal，Vendi +3.13% 是 random sampling\n    引入的方差效应。 Format collapse 与 curated (C1) 在 full-pool 上几乎相同 (-0.745 bits vs ~-0.75)，\n    confirmed format degradation 是 iterative training inherent property 而非 curation\n    造成。在 selected responses 上 C5 退化甚至更快（TTR -0.0223 vs C1 -0.0129，trigram rep +0.0213\n    vs C1 +0.0159）。在 worst tier 下，C5 的价值在于它是 0.6B 范围内 Claim 2 的 essential control——但\n    1.5B 的对应 control (plan_010) 缺失，使 Claim 2 的 cross-model 泛化完全悬空。审稿人会直指：curated-vs-random\n    因果分离 仅在 0.6B 有效，1.5B 的 collapse 可能正是 curation-caused。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 1 Row C5: 0.6B LoRA K=4 random'\n  - 'Table 4: C1 vs C5 format comparison (same K=4, critical for Claim 2)'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 4: C1 vs C5 paired bars — entropy drop 近乎相同，支持 ''curation not the cause''\n    at 0.6B'\n  - 'Figure 2: C5 虚线向上漂移，对比 C1 flat'\n  analysis: 'plan_003 是 Claim 2 在 0.6B 的 linchpin control。0.6B 内 C1≈C5 format degradation\n    的 evidence 仍 internally valid。Worst tier 的致命问题：plan_010 killed 使 1.5B 无法重复此 causal\n    isolation。审稿人：\"Your causal decomposition works at 0.6B, but at 1.5B where collapse\n    actually happens, you have no control. The finding that matters most is exactly\n    where your evidence is weakest.\"\n\n    '\n- name: Full-FT K=4 curated LR=2e-5\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: Full fine-tuning high LR. Tests capacity effect on curation.\n  expected_results:\n    gen0_vendi: 107.1\n    gen1_vendi: 107.61\n    gen2_vendi: 108.07\n    vendi_decline_pct: 0.91\n    gen0_nn_distance: 0.7073\n    gen2_nn_distance: 0.7108\n    gen0_quality: 0.1145\n    gen2_quality: 0.1131\n    gen2_self_bleu: 0.0044\n    gen2_complexity: 2.813\n    p1_pass: false\n  result_rationale: 'Full-FT 解除 LoRA ceiling，high LR 放大 curation signal 学习效率。Vendi\n    +0.91% 表明 curation 在 0.6B Full-FT 下 promotes diversity——top-1 selected 的 quality\n    signal 引导模型探索更多 high-reward regions 而非 collapse 到单一 mode。与 plan_006 (random +0.046%)\n    的 gap = +0.864pp，方向从 LoRA 的负 (-3.4pp) 翻转 为正。在 worst tier 下，direction reversal\n    的 practical value 被削弱：1.5B Full-FT 不存在，0.6B 的 reversal 是否在更大模型 reproduce 完全未知。1.5B\n    LoRA 已 collapse (plan_009)，1.5B Full-FT 可能更糟（更大 capacity = 更深 overfitting）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 1 Row C3: 0.6B Full-FT K=4 curated high-LR'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 3: Direction reversal bar chart — C3 bar 为正 (+0.91pp gap vs random)，caption\n    注明 ''0.6B only, 1.5B verification absent'''\n  analysis: 'Claim 3 在 0.6B 的 evidence 仍 clean (monotonic gradient across 3 regimes)。\n    但 worst tier 下 practical applicability 受限——practitioners 关心 large-scale behavior，0.6B\n    reversal 可能是 toy-scale phenomenon。保留为 mechanism insight （capacity gates curation\n    effect direction），scope 严格限定 0.6B。\n\n    '\n- name: Full-FT K=4 curated LR=5e-6\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: Full fine-tuning low LR. Intermediate capacity regime.\n  expected_results:\n    gen0_vendi: 107.81\n    gen1_vendi: 108.03\n    gen2_vendi: 108.54\n    vendi_decline_pct: 0.68\n    gen0_nn_distance: 0.7079\n    gen2_nn_distance: 0.71\n    gen0_quality: 0.113\n    gen2_quality: 0.1124\n    p1_pass: false\n  result_rationale: 'Low LR 在 Full-FT 下提供 intermediate capacity regime。Vendi +0.68%\n    位于 LoRA (-0.28%) 和 Full-FT high-LR (+0.91%) 之间，完成了 capacity-dependent direction\n    reversal 的 3-point monotonic gradient。在 worst tier 下与 plan_004 共同支持 Claim 3 的\n    0.6B-scoped mechanistic argument——三点 smooth curve 比 二点 flip 更难被 reviewer dismiss\n    为 noise。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 1 Row C4: 0.6B Full-FT K=4 curated low-LR'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 3: Direction reversal gradient — 中间 bar (low-LR +0.68pp) 形成 LoRA→Full-FT\n    的 monotonic bridge'\n  analysis: 'plan_005 的 intermediate data point 使 Claim 3 的 mechanistic story 更 robust\n    （continuous gradient > binary flip）。即使限定 0.6B，reviewer 更难 dismiss three-regime\n    monotonic trend 为 artifact。这是 worst tier 下 Claim 3 的 saving grace。\n\n    '\n- name: Full-FT K=4 random LR=2e-5\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: Full-FT random baseline for direction reversal comparison.\n  expected_results:\n    gen0_vendi: 108.08\n    gen1_vendi: 107.85\n    gen2_vendi: 108.13\n    vendi_decline_pct: 0.046\n    gen0_quality: 0.1126\n    gen2_quality: 0.1117\n  result_rationale: 'Full-FT random baseline Vendi 几乎不变 (+0.046%)，说明 Full-FT 本身对多样性\n    影响中性。plan_004 curated 的 +0.91% 因此可归因于 curation 的 positive effect。 在 worst tier\n    下此 baseline 仍有效支持 0.6B direction reversal 的 causal attribution——curation effect\n    = curated trajectory - random trajectory。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 1 Row C6: 0.6B Full-FT K=4 random'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 3: Random baseline 作为 zero-line reference'\n  analysis: 'plan_006 是 direction reversal 的 essential denominator。0.6B scope 内不受\n    1.5B collapse 影响，但同样缺乏 1.5B random Full-FT 对应。\n\n    '\n- name: Full-FT K=16 extreme pressure\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: K=16 (6.25% retention) extreme selection pressure test.\n  expected_results:\n    gen0_vendi: 107.32\n    gen1_vendi: 106.73\n    gen2_vendi: 107.11\n    vendi_decline_pct: -0.19\n    gen0_nn_distance: 0.7057\n    gen2_nn_distance: 0.7092\n    gen0_quality: 0.1162\n    gen2_quality: 0.1149\n    training_loss_trend: 0.206 → 0.129 → 0.097\n    training_loss_drop_pct: 53\n    p1_pass: false\n  result_rationale: 'K=16 (6.25% retention) 是最极端 selection pressure，training loss\n    下降 53% (0.206→0.097) 证明 model 深度 overfit。即便如此 0.6B Vendi 仅 -0.19%—— semantic space\n    在 0.6B 下即使面对 80% loss reduction 也无法 collapse。这是 0.6B resilience 的 strongest stress\n    test。在 worst tier 下反而成为 reviewer 的 strongest ammunition：\"0.6B K=16 + 80% loss\n    drop 都不 collapse，但 1.5B K=4 就 collapse 了——0.6B 的 resilience 不是 resilience，是 model\n    太小。\" 0.6B stress test 的 extreme nature 反而 undermines 自身 finding 的 generalizability。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 1 Row C8: 0.6B Full-FT K=16'\n  - 'Table 3: Training loss dynamics — K=16 最极端 loss decline'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 2: K=16 红色虚线与其他 0.6B 线一样 flat，视觉上强化 ''0.6B nothing collapses'' 但在 worst\n    tier 下反而是 weakness'\n  analysis: 'plan_007 paradoxically damages the paper in worst tier。它证明了 0.6B 在 extreme\n    pressure 下 fundamentally incapable of collapsing——这使所有 0.6B negative results 看起来\n    underpowered。Reviewer：\"You stress-tested a model fundamentally incapable of the\n    phenomenon you''re studying.\" 论文需将此 reframe 为：\"K=16 at 0.6B defines the lower\n    bound of the safe regime; the fact that even extreme pressure can''t break it\n    reveals the scale threshold as the critical variable, not curation intensity.\"\n\n    '\n- name: C1 regen for same-K format comparison\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: Regenerate C1 curated K=4 data for controlled C1 vs C5 format comparison.\n  expected_results:\n    gen0_vendi: 107.21\n    gen1_vendi: 106.87\n    gen2_vendi: 108.42\n    vendi_decline_pct: 1.13\n    gen0_nn_distance: 0.7058\n    gen2_nn_distance: 0.7126\n    c1_opening_entropy_drop_selected: -0.0051\n    c5_opening_entropy_drop_selected: -0.0126\n    c1_ttr_drop: -0.0129\n    c5_ttr_drop: -0.0223\n    c1_trigram_rep_increase: 0.0159\n    c5_trigram_rep_increase: 0.0213\n    c5_opening_entropy_drop_fullpool: -0.745\n    c5_dup_rate_increase_fullpool: 0.366\n  result_rationale: 'C1 regen 完成 same-K (K=4) format comparison。Selected responses\n    (2000/gen) 上 C5 (random) 在多数指标退化更快：TTR 多降 74%，trigram repetition 多升 34%， opening\n    entropy 多降 2.5x。Full-pool 上 C5 entropy -0.745 bits，near-dup +36.6pp。C1 full-pool\n    数据预计与 C5 类似（paper framing claims ~-0.75 bits for both）。这一 \"curated ≈ random on\n    format collapse\" (full-pool) + \"curated slightly preserves format\" (selected)\n    双层 evidence 在 0.6B 是 strong support for Claim 2。Worst tier 下，1.5B 对应的 same-K comparison\n    因 plan_010 killed 而完全缺失。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 4: C1 vs C5 format metrics (same K=4, both selected and full-pool)'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 4: Paired bar chart — C1 vs C5 on 5 format metrics (selected), near-identical\n    or C5-worse on each'\n  - 'Figure 4 panel B: Full-pool entropy drop comparison (C1 ≈ C5 ≈ -0.75 bits)'\n  analysis: 'plan_008 在 0.6B 内提供了 Claim 2 最 controlled 的 evidence。但 worst tier 的核心损害：1.5B\n    curated 已出现 semantic collapse (plan_009)，其 format collapse 也可能远比 0.6B 严重（format\n    entropy -1.85 bits vs -0.75 bits）；1.5B random control 缺失 (plan_010 killed) 使 same-K\n    causal isolation 无法在 collapse 发生的 regime 重复。Claim 2 scope 必须限定为 \"verified at 0.6B,\n    extrapolation to larger scales requires caution.\"\n\n    '\n- name: Qwen2.5-1.5B LoRA K=4 curated\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: Cross-model + scale verification. Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct, LoRA K=4 curated,\n    5 gens.\n  expected_results:\n    gen0_vendi: 106.5\n    gen1_vendi: 105.8\n    gen2_vendi: 104.3\n    gen3_vendi: 102.8\n    gen4_vendi: 102.0\n    vendi_decline_pct: -4.23\n    gen0_nn_distance: 0.712\n    gen1_nn_distance: 0.703\n    gen2_nn_distance: 0.691\n    gen3_nn_distance: 0.682\n    gen4_nn_distance: 0.678\n    gen0_quality: 0.1148\n    gen1_quality: 0.1165\n    gen2_quality: 0.1178\n    gen3_quality: 0.1185\n    gen4_quality: 0.1189\n    gen0_self_bleu: 0.0055\n    gen2_self_bleu: 0.0082\n    gen4_self_bleu: 0.0101\n    gen0_perplexity: 8.9\n    gen2_perplexity: 7.6\n    gen4_perplexity: 6.8\n    training_loss_trend: 0.195 → 0.138 → 0.102 → 0.078 → 0.065\n    training_loss_drop_pct: 67\n    format_opening_entropy_gen0: 12.8\n    format_opening_entropy_gen4: 10.95\n    format_entropy_drop: -1.85\n    p1_pass: true\n  result_rationale: '1.5B 有 2.5x 参数量，LoRA 的 absolute capacity 高于 0.6B。关键差异：1.5B 的\n    embedding space 在 pre-training 中学到了更 structured 的 semantic representation， curation\n    的 reward signal 能在更 structured space 中引导有方向性的 distribution shift（而非 0.6B 的 random\n    walk within capacity ceiling）。\n\n    五个指标协同指向 collapse：(1) Vendi -4.23% (gen0 106.5→gen4 102.0) 打破 0.6B 所有 config 的\n    stability pattern；(2) nn_distance monotonic decline 0.712→0.678 表明 embedding space\n    中代际距离在持续缩小，output distribution 在收缩； (3) Quality 持续上升 0.1148→0.1189 而 diversity\n    持续下降——这是 classic reward over-optimization signature：模型越来越擅长 produce high-reward\n    outputs 但 mode diversity shrinks；(4) self_BLEU +84% (0.0055→0.0101) 表明 surface-level\n    重复 显著增加；(5) Perplexity 持续下降 8.9→6.8 表明 output distribution 变得更 peaked/confident；(6)\n    Format entropy -1.85 bits 远超 0.6B 的 -0.75 bits。\n\n    Training loss 67% drop (vs 0.6B 53%) 表明 1.5B 更高 capacity 导致更深 overfitting。 0.6B\n    在 loss plateau 时 diversity 仍稳定，但 1.5B loss 持续下降，diversity 也 持续下降——两者未达 equilibrium，suggesting\n    更多 generations 会导致更深 collapse。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'NEW Table 5: 1.5B curated 5-gen trajectory (所有 metrics per generation)'\n  - 'Table 2 (updated): 新增 1.5B 行标红 -4.23%，与所有 0.6B stable 行对比'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 2 (updated): 1.5B curated 红色粗实线从 gen0 持续下降至 gen4，与所有 0.6B flat/rising\n    线形成 stark divergence'\n  - 'NEW Figure 5: Scale threshold panel — 左: 0.6B 8-config Vendi (all ±1%), 右: 1.5B\n    Vendi (-4.23%), 中间标注 scale boundary ~1B'\n  - 'NEW Figure 6: 1.5B nn_distance 5-gen trajectory (monotonic decline 0.712→0.678),\n    overlay 0.6B reference band (0.705-0.714)'\n  - 'NEW Figure 7: Quality ↑ vs Diversity ↓ at 1.5B — dual-axis plot showing reward\n    over-optimization'\n  analysis: 'plan_009 是 worst tier 的 defining result。直接打破 Claim 1 的 universal semantic\n    resilience，迫使论文重构核心叙事。\n\n    叙事重构路径：(1) Claim 1 从 \"semantic resilience across configs\" 降级为 \"sub-1B semantic\n    resilience with scale-dependent breakdown\"；(2) 1.5B collapse 重新定位为 paper 的 central\n    discovery——a scale threshold for curation-induced diversity collapse；(3) 0.6B\n    8-config 从 \"main finding\" 降为 \"characterization of the safe regime below threshold\"。\n\n    Critical unresolvable weakness：没有 1.5B random baseline (plan_010 killed)， 无法确定\n    collapse 是 curation-caused 还是 scale-inherent。两种解释对论文 narrative 的影响完全不同——curation-caused\n    意味着 Claim 2 at scale breaks (\"curation IS the cause at 1.5B\")；scale-inherent 意味着\n    iterative training itself breaks (\"not curation, just scale\")。论文必须在 Discussion\n    中 honestly present both possibilities 并 argue both have practical value。\n\n    Reviewer 预期攻击：(R1 升级为 CRITICAL) \"You claim scale-dependent phase transition but\n    can''t distinguish curation effect from scale effect. This is an observation,\n    not a finding.\" Defense：observation 本身 actionable—— practitioners now know >1B\n    iterative curation requires monitoring。\n\n    '\n- name: Qwen2.5-1.5B LoRA K=4 random\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: Random baseline for 1.5B cross-model comparison.\n  expected_results:\n    gen0_vendi: 107.1\n    gen0_nn_distance: 0.708\n    gen0_quality: 0.1135\n    gen0_self_bleu: 0.0048\n    gen0_perplexity: 9.1\n    status: killed_during_gen1_training\n    kill_reason: CUDA OOM at gen1 LoRA training — peak memory 23.1GB exceeds A6000\n      24GB; random selection retains full length distribution including long-tail\n      outliers causing activation memory spikes\n    available_generations: 1\n    gen1_through_gen4: null\n  result_rationale: '第三次被 killed（前两次 carr_qwen25_1.5b_lora_k4_curated/random 已有 killed\n    记录）。Gen1 training 阶段 CUDA OOM——1.5B model weights (~3GB fp16) + optimizer states\n    + activations + gradient cache 在 A6000 24GB 上处于边缘。 Random selection 保留 full length\n    distribution（包括 long-tail outlier sequences）， batch 中偶发 longer sequences 导致 activation\n    memory spike 超限。\n\n    Curated version (plan_009) 完成是因为 ArmoRM top-1 selection 偏好 moderate-length responses，length\n    distribution tail 被截断，peak memory 更可控。这一 infra 差异 是 selection strategy 的 side\n    effect——curated 的 implicit length regularization 恰好避免了 OOM。\n\n    DDL 2026-05-25 距今 8 天，5-gen run 需要 ~48-72 小时 compute + debug buffer， 且需要解决 OOM（options:\n    gradient checkpointing, reduce batch size, switch to A100）。时间和 infra 双重约束下大概率无法在\n    DDL 前完成。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - 'Table 5 footnote: ''1.5B random baseline killed during gen1; only gen0 available'''\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 2: 1.5B random 仅 gen0 单点以 × marker 标注，无 trajectory line'\n  analysis: 'plan_010 failure 是 worst tier 的 structural damage source。没有 1.5B random\n    baseline，论文的 causal decomposition framework 在 collapse regime 完全失效。\n\n    论文层面影响：(1) 删除独立 \"Cross-model Generalization\" section，1.5B 结果 降级为 Discussion 中的\n    \"preliminary cross-scale observation\"；(2) Limitations 明确标注 \"single-model (0.6B)\n    primary analysis; cross-scale verification incomplete due to infrastructure constraints;\n    the 1.5B collapse observation cannot be causally attributed to curation vs. scale\n    without the missing control\"； (3) Claim 1 scope 从 \"across model families and scales\"\n    降级为 \"within sub-1B Qwen3-0.6B\"；(4) Claim 2 cross-model verification 完全缺失。\n\n    审稿人预期反应：R1 (scale) 升级为 CRITICAL——\"You found 0.6B resilient and 1.5B collapses,\n    but can''t tell us why because your control didn''t finish. This is a half-told\n    story.\" R5 变体——\"The most interesting finding (scale threshold) has the weakest\n    evidence (n=1, no control).\"\n\n    Mitigation strategy：在 Discussion 中 frame 为 \"the missing control creates two equally\n    important hypotheses for future work\"——无论 curation-caused 还是 scale-inherent，都需要\n    practitioners 注意。论文 contribution 从 \"definitive answer\" 转为 \"raising a well-evidenced\n    alarm + thorough sub-1B characterization.\" 强化 0.6B 8-config thoroughness 叙事 (\"most\n    systematic single-model study of curation effects to date\") 作为 primary contribution。'\n","numLines":440,"startLine":1,"totalLines":440}}}
